ocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T10:02:01-08:00","id":1059585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1057825-all-night-horror-books?p=1059577#post1059577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I never actually read any of the clan books (IIRC, a lot of the fonts were just too hard for me to read with how bad my eyes are), but in skimming them at the bookstore (remember those?), the Count was one of the things that stood out enough for me to remember.<br /> <br /> Every clan should have their own Dracula, IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always liked that in the back of the Ordo Dracul book, it had the three pretender Draculas: &quot;Hollywood Drac&quot;, &quot;The Gilded Fireplug&quot;, and &quot;The Romanian Terror&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T10:18:27-08:00","id":1059594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1057825-all-night-horror-books?p=1059585#post1059585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I always liked that in the back of the Ordo Dracul book, it had the three pretender Draculas: &quot;Hollywood Drac&quot;, &quot;The Gilded Fireplug&quot;, and &quot;The Romanian Terror&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>As did I. <br /> <br /> I wonder if you could do an entire Night Horror book of just versions of Dracula.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T10:35:39-08:00","id":1059603,"title":"","content":"I'd be more interested in his brides. The first ones, not the biker gang, though that is a cool covenant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T10:59:12-08:00","id":1059610,"title":"","content":"The historical Dracula and the Order he was a part of, his mortal bloodline, reincarnations, the original Stoker character as presented in the book along with his brides, Mina Harker as some sort of carious of his curse, the &quot;took over Britain&quot; alternate Victorian Age from Anno Dracul, the classic movie version, Dracula captured by Nazis and used to create vampiric super soldiers in WW2, Blacula, the camp version from the 60s/70s, the heir of ancient Atlantean curse from Marvel Comics, the &quot;Dracula as modern day power broker&quot; version that popped up a little in the late 80s and early 90s, the romantic tragi-goth version, cyberpunk Dracula whose soul is trapped in the web as a killer virus, alien space Dracula ...<br /> <br /> I've always found the Brides interesting. I liked the treatment of them in Ordo Dracul. But I'm sort of surprised you don't see more fiction about them. (Maybe they'll play a larger role in this shared cinematic universe thing Universal is doing.)<br /> <br /> I imagine in Requiem you could easily work out as many multiple versions of the Brides as you could the Count. I have this image in my head of some sort of all female monastic order of vampire nuns who see themselves as Brides of Dracula the same way Catholic nuns see themselves as Brides of Christ. I'm just not sure if Dracula-Christ is supposed to save their souls or satiate their hunger by giving them tasty babies to eat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T11:06:40-08:00","id":1059614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1057825-all-night-horror-books?p=1059610#post1059610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine in Requiem you could easily work out as many multiple versions of the Brides as you could the Count. I have this image in my head of some sort of all female monastic order of vampire nuns who see themselves as Brides of Dracula the same way Catholic nuns see themselves as Brides of Christ. I'm just not sure if Dracula-Christ is supposed to save their souls or satiate their hunger by giving them tasty babies to eat.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's the aforementioned biker gang covenant, called the Brides of Dracula. Despite the name they are not all female.<br /> <br /> Offhand I'd say that Requiem tries not to revolve its organizations around individual figures. They tend to be part of the background, then fade into history. It's possible the Crone, Longinus and Dracula are out there manipulating things but most games will focus more on the here and now.<br /> <br /> That said, we'll probably see age-old manipulators in the upcoming Thousand Years of Night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T11:36:34-08:00","id":1059635,"title":"","content":"I was thinking they'd be some sort of deranged heretical cult whose members have never actually met a Dracula but believe in him anyway. <br /> <br /> Perhaps with a Japanese offshoot that celebrate Christmas by dressing a statute of Colonel Sanders up in a Bela Legosi cape. Or maybe that would be just <i>too</i> ridiculous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T15:01:04-08:00","id":1059768,"title":"","content":"It's only ridiculous until the funny-looking guy sprouts unholy fangs and starts to stalk you in the night.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Dracula (and his many, <i>many </i>iterations), I wonder if we can do something similar for all other monster types. Depictions of the &quot;archetypical&quot; characters of literature and other media that inspired each gameline, and how they'd fit in the worlds. We already have (lots of) Dracula in Requiem, and the original Frankenstein's Monster in Promethean. What could we get out of other games?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T15:41:02-08:00","id":1059794,"title":"","content":"I believe wyrdhamster did something with Thiess of Kaltenbrun and the 'hounds of God.' and of course the writers have incorporated the myth of Lycaon into several places in the werewolf setting.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't look for a Larry Talbot, the first 'Wolf Man' in werewolf, but you can find it in the Talbot House in Hunter the Vigil. They try to pray the wolf away.<br /> <br /> Various other wolf myths are scattered throughout the setting, Fenris being a Firstborn along with the Dire Wolf. And since its incorporated into the spirit there's other myths as well, from King Solomon the Magician to Ammut from ancient Egypt and, later, Mummy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-07-2017, 08:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T17:12:07-08:00","id":1059832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1057825-all-night-horror-books?p=1059768#post1059768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's only ridiculous until the funny-looking guy sprouts unholy fangs and starts to stalk you in the night.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Dracula (and his many, <i>many </i>iterations), I wonder if we can do something similar for all other monster types. Depictions of the &quot;archetypical&quot; characters of literature and other media that inspired each gameline, and how they'd fit in the worlds. We already have (lots of) Dracula in Requiem, and the original Frankenstein's Monster in Promethean. What could we get out of other games?</div> </div> </div> </div>Can't think of one for Werewolf...<br /> <br /> Merlin for Mage seems like a gimme; Dave had a really cool rundown of what that might be like.<br /> <br /> Puck for Changeling, perhaps. There are a lot of iconic fairy tale characters to draw from.<br /> <br /> Hunter is a bit trickier because they don't tend to live long enough for this sort of thing...unless you make Van Helsing an independent ghoul of some sort.<br /> <br /> I imagine there are a lot of characters you could drawn on for Geist, but I can't think of any off the top of my head.<br /> <br /> No idea for Mummy. A lot of them are Egyptian kings, which doesn't fit the cosmology.<br /> <br /> Lucifer for Demon...or any number of named demons from Christian apocrypha and Middle Eastern mythology.<br /> <br /> Beast could have any big name monster you can think of. Grendel would be a good one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 03-07-2017, 08:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T19:01:49-08:00","id":1059876,"title":"","content":"I'd have to think about Frankenstein, since Promethean's groups already hit a bunch of the classic takes, including modern cloning. <br /> <br /> For Hunter, there's Nimrod, Hercules and other Greek heroes, St. George the Dragon Slayer (already sort of covered), the woodsman from Red Riding Hood, Van Helsing, <br /> <br /> I'm not very familiar with Beast, but Leviathan and Behemoth, maybe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T12:44:22-08:00","id":1060230,"title":"","content":"Nimrod and Hercules strike me more as Heroes, but the line is pretty thin sometimes","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T12:49:27-08:00","id":1060235,"title":"","content":"Nimrod was actually stated to be a possible Slasher, not hunter. Nimrod being reborn was also a possible plot hook, I believe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T14:52:22-08:00","id":1060291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1057825-all-night-horror-books?p=1059794#post1059794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe wyrdhamster did something with Thiess of Kaltenbrun and the 'hounds of God.' and of course the writers have incorporated the myth of Lycaon into several places in the werewolf setting.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't look for a Larry Talbot, the first 'Wolf Man' in werewolf, but you can find it in the Talbot House in Hunter the Vigil. They try to pray the wolf away.<br /> <br /> Various other wolf myths are scattered throughout the setting, Fenris being a Firstborn along with the Dire Wolf. And since its incorporated into the spirit there's other myths as well, from King Solomon the Magician to Ammut from ancient Egypt and, later, Mummy.</div> </div> </div> </div> <b><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vseslav_of_Polotsk\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Vseslav of Polotsk springs to mind</span></span></b></a></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bisclavret\" target=\"_blank\">Bisclavret</a>/Sir Marrock is a great crossover character for werewolf and mage as a knight of the round table, and thus the one werewolf who would have been there for Camelot before the exarchs retconned it</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> and then you have the resident werewolf in my neck of the woods, <a href=\"http://weekinweird.com/2016/01/31/silver-bullets-in-talbot-county-the-strange-grave-of-emily-isabella-burt-georgias-real-life-werewolf/\" target=\"_blank\">Emily Isabella Burt</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 03-08-2017, 06:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}